---
description: Use pnpm and Node.js. Do not use Bun, npm, or yarn.
globs: "*.ts, *.tsx, *.html, *.css, *.js, *.jsx, package.json"
alwaysApply: false
---

Use pnpm as the package manager and Node.js as the runtime. Do not use Bun, npm, or yarn.

- Use `node <file>` or `npx ts-node <file>` to run files, not `bun <file>`
- Use `pnpm install` instead of `npm install`, `yarn install`, or `bun install`
- Use `pnpm run <script>` instead of `npm run`, `yarn run`, or `bun run`
- Use `pnpm add <package>` instead of `npm install <package>` or `bun add`
- Use `pnpm remove <package>` instead of `npm uninstall` or `bun remove`
- Use `dotenv` or `dotenv-flow` to load `.env` files — Node.js does not load them automatically
- Do not reference `bun:*` imports or `Bun.*` globals
